      'Rule example: Score more points than your opponent by winning tricks (card points plus last-trick bonus) and declaring buongiochi (three or four of a rank, or Napoletana 3-2-A of a suit). The game ends when a player reaches 51 or more points.',
      'Turn-flow example: Two players play 20 tricks. Non-dealer leads first; winner of each trick leads the next. You may play from your hand or the top of one of your two face-up packets (revealing the next card). Must follow suit when possible. Same suit: higher card wins; different suit: lead wins. Honours (3, 2, Ace) on top of a packet may be moved to hand. Declare buongiochi (three or four of same rank, or Napoletana 3-2-A of a suit) when acquired to score 3 or 4 points. After 20 tricks, count card points in tricks won plus 1 for last trick; add meld points. Game ends when a player reaches 51 points.',
